ne linen, of the house of Ashbea,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆand Jokim, and the men of Chozeba, and Joash, and Saraph, who had the dominion in Moab, and Jashubi-lehem. And these are ancient things.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrThese were the potters, and those that dwelt among plants and hedges: there they dwelt with the king for his work.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDThe sons of Simeon were, Nemuel, and Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, and Shaul:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ0Shallum his son, Mibsam his son, Mishma his son.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHAnd the sons of Mishma; Hamuel his son, Zacchur his son, Shimei his son.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœAnd Shimei had sixteen sons and six daughters; but his brethren had not many children, neither did all their family multiply, like to the children of Judah.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse&¦verses›„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ;And they dwelt at Beer-sheba, and Moladah, and Hazar-shual,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ)and at Bilhah, and at Ezem, and at Tolad,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ-and at Bethuel, and at Hormah, and at Ziklag,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|and at Beth-marcaboth, and Hazar-susim, and at Beth-birei, and at Shaaraim. These were their cities unto the reign of David.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSAnd their villages were, Etam, and Ain, Rimmon, and Tochen, and Ashan, five cities:¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{and all their villages that were round about the same cities, unto Baal. These were their habitations, and their genealogy.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9And Meshobab, and Jamlech, and Joshah the son of Amaziah,¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMand Joel, and Jehu the son of Josibiah, the son of Seraiah, the son of Asiel,¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]and Elioenai, and Jaakobah, and Jeshohaiah, and Asaiah, and Adiel, and Jesimiel, and Benaiah,¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiand Ziza the son of Shiphi, the son of Allon, the son of Jedaiah, the son of Shimri, the son of Shemaiah;¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpthese mentioned by their names were princes in their families: and the house of their fathers increased greatly.¦layout ªlast_verse&…¤book§chapter«first_verse'ªlast_verse)¦verses“„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpAnd they went to the entrance of Gedor, even unto the east side of the valley, to seek pasture for their flocks.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}And they found fat pasture and good, and the land was wide, and quiet, and peaceable; for they of Ham had dwelt there of old.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙıAnd these written by name came in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah, and smote their tents, and the habitations that were found there, and destroyed them utterly unto this day, and dwelt in their rooms: because there was pasture there for their flocks.¦layout ªlast_verse)…¤book§chapter«first_verse*ªlast_verse+¦verses’„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ°And some of them, even of the sons of Simeon, five hundred men, went to mount Seir, having for their captains Pelatiah, and Neariah, and Rephaiah, and Uzziel, the sons of Ishi.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[And they smote the rest of the Amalekites that were escaped, and dwelt there unto this day.¦layout ªlast_verse+